  "title": "Franco-American alliance and Treaty of Amity and Commerce",
  "summary": "On 6 February 1778 the American colonies and France signed a military Treaty of Alliance at Paris, formalizing French financial and military support for the revolutionary government. A companion Treaty of Amity and Commerce promoted trade and recognized the United States as an independent nation. The alliance barred either party from making a separate peace with Britain.",
